<article class="env-lemma" id="065S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/065S">Lemma <span data-tag="065S">10.109.9</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $0 \to M' \to M \to M'' \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of $R$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $M$ has projective dimension $\leq n$ and $M''$ has projective dimension $\leq n + 1$, then $M'$ has projective dimension $\leq n$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $M'$ and $M''$ have projective dimension $\leq n$ then $M$ has projective dimension $\leq n$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $M'$ has projective dimension $\leq n$ and $M$ has projective dimension $\leq n + 1$ then $M''$ has projective dimension $\leq n + 1$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine the characterization of projective dimension in Lemma <a href="/tag/065R" data-tag="065R">10.109.8</a> with the long exact sequence of ext groups in Lemma <a href="/tag/065P" data-tag="065P">10.71.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>